INT. FLOODED CHURCH CRYPT - COMMAND POST - NIGHT

Vaulted brick. Knee-deep water. A table on cinderblocks, a field telephone, three lanterns. Mortar dust drifts down with each distant shell.

MAJOR WINIFRED BAPTISTE-OKONKWO (40s, helmet off, tired) leans over a map.

CAPTAIN LUCIAN HARGREAVES-DIALLO (30s, bandaged forehead) sits on the table edge.

SERGEANT EUSTACE "STACKS" WILLOUGHBY (50s, immense, silent) cleans a rifle.

LIEUTENANT SIMONE ARCHAMBAULT-TSOSIE (20s, radio operator) crouches by the field telephone.

CORPORAL REUBEN VASQUEZ-OLUWOLE (20s, sentry) watches the stairs.

The field telephone buzzes. Simone grabs it.

SIMONE
Command post.

COLONEL (V.O.)
(over the phone, thin)
Status.

SIMONE
Holding, sir. Water's rising.

COLONEL (V.O.)
Hold until dawn.

SIMONE
Sir, they're shelling the nave.

COLONEL (V.O.)
Hold until dawn, Lieutenant.

The line clicks. Simone lowers the receiver.

WINIFRED
Well?

SIMONE
Dawn.

LUCIAN
That's five hours.

WINIFRED
Then we'll see five hours.

A shell hits the church. The crypt shakes. Mortar rains. A lantern swings, throws shadows.

REUBEN
(muttering)
Closer. Closer.

STACKS
(rumble)
Let them.

Winifred and Lucian step aside, water sloshing. They whisper over the map.

WINIFRED
If the north wall goes, we pull back through the ossuary.

LUCIAN
And if the ossuary floods?

WINIFRED
Then we swim.

A third shell, so close the lanterns gutter. Reuben shouts from the stairs.

REUBEN
Movement! Top step!

Everyone drops. Rifles up. Stacks rolls behind the table. Simone drags the phone under it.

A boot appears on the stairs. Then a hand, empty, open.

WINIFRED
Hold fire!

LUCIAN ^
Hold fire!

Nobody fires. A voice, thin and foreign, from the dark above.

REUBEN
(calling up)
Show yourself!

The crypt shakes one more time. Then, for the first time in hours, silence.

STACKS
(low)
That's the barrage ending.

Dust settles. Water stills. Reuben lowers his rifle at last.

WINIFRED
(to the whole crypt)
Stand down. Rest in shifts.

LUCIAN
Dawn?

WINIFRED
Dawn.

She turns to the map and does not look back at the stairs.
